<title>UK: Deutsche Bank sets 10 billion yen two-year bond.</title>
<headline>Deutsche Bank sets 10 billion yen two-year bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by lead manager Deutsche Morgan Grenfell.</p>
<p> BORROWER   DEUTSCHE BANK AG LONDON</p>
<p> AMT    10 BLN YEN    COUPON    *4.20 PCT  MATURITY    21.DEC.98</p>
<p> TYPE   STRAIGHT	ISS PRICE  100.125   PAY DATE  L-19.DEC.96</p>
<p> FULL FEES  0.125     REOFFER    =	   L-LONG LAST COUPON</p>
<p> MOODY	AAA	 LISTING    NONE	PAY FREQ    =</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  AAA	 DENOMS (K) 100	 SALE LIMITS =</p>
<p> NOTES     *REDEMPTION WILL BE EITHER IN YEN OR U.S. DOLLARS</p>
<p>		AT A RATE OF $877.57 PER YEN 100,000 NOTE.</p>
<p>		ISSUED UNDER AN MTN PROGRAMME.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
